 and prediction markets both point to a modest but real Hill lead.", "watch": "New polling showing Jones ahead or a late Democratic turnout surge in Pulaski County would move this toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent French Hill (R) is running."]}, "overview": "French Hill seeks another term in a central Arkansas district that leans Republican by about eight points, while Democrat Chris Jones has run a well-funded challenge that has drawn national attention. Hill holds a clear financial advantage, having raised more than five million dollars with nearly 1.5 million on hand, and outside groups have added to his support. Most race ratings call the district Likely Republican, with a couple placing it at Lean Republican.\n\nPolling is sparse and mixed. An Emerson College survey in mid-October put Hill ahead 52 to 48 among likely voters, while an August Hendrix College poll had Jones up four points. Prediction markets give Jones roughly an 18 percent chance of winning. The combined picture points to a modest Hill lead, with enough uncertainty that a strong Democratic environment could still make this close.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3205, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3445, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2683, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2648, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2693, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2922, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0